# zig-only
# A split divider dragged to a column settles on that column, not one
# short of it. With the tree at 30 the panes span x=31..119 (89 cells);
# the fresh split's divider is at x=75 and the left pane's text starts
# at x=36, so the cell left of a divider at x=100 is (99-36)%10 = 3.
write a.txt 0123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789\nsecond
open a.txt
command view.split_right
expect screen contains "45678│   1 01234567890"
drag 75 10 100 10
expect screen contains "90123│   1 01234567890"
drag 100 10 60 10
expect screen contains "0123│   1 012345678901234567890123456789"
drag 60 10 90 10
expect screen contains "0123│   1 01234567890"
expect screen lacks "9012│"
